diff --git a/Documentation/hydrogenx-v11-schedutil-pissarro.rst b/Documentation/hydrogenx-v11-schedutil-pissarro.rst
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..000000000000
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/hydrogenx-v11-schedutil-pissarro.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+HydrogenX v11 schedutil patch for pissarro
+============================================
+
+What changed
+------------
+
+HydrogenX v11 removes the earlier dbs/ondemand style governor and replaces it
+with a scheduler driven governor named ``hydrogenx``.  The new governor lives
+under ``kernel/sched/cpufreq_hydrogen_schedutil.c`` and is wired through
+``kernel/sched/Makefile``.  It keeps schedutil's update-util callback model and
+adds HydrogenX scene floors around the final frequency decision.
+
+Why this is stronger than the old HydrogenX
+-------------------------------------------
+
+The old HydrogenX sampled CPU load through the generic dbs governor core.  That
+was easy to tune, but it did not truly inherit schedutil's scheduler coupling.
+The v11 governor is based on the same kind of scheduler callback path as
+``cpufreq_schedutil.c``: the scheduler calls into the governor when utilization
+changes.  That keeps PELT/WALT utilization, IO-wait boosting, RT/deadline fast
+maximum frequency behavior, and fast-switch support when the cpufreq driver can
+do it.
+
+HydrogenX additions
+-------------------
+
+The global controller remains under ``/sys/kernel/hydrogenx``.  It provides
+``profile``, ``game_mode``, ``floor_freq``, ``floor_pct``, ``boost_floor_pct``,
+``sched_boost``, ``uclamp_min``, ``input_hook``, ``boostpulse``,
+``input_boostpulse``, ``frame_boost``, ``gpu_boost``, ``ddr_boost`` and
+``io_boost``.
+
+The per-policy governor tunables are under each policy's ``hydrogenx``
+directory when governor-per-policy sysfs is enabled.  Important tunables are
+``up_rate_limit_us``, ``down_rate_limit_us``, ``down_hold_us``,
+``hispeed_load``, ``hispeed_freq``, ``floor_pct``, ``game_min_freq``,
+``frame_min_freq``, ``boost_floor_pct``, ``powersave_bias``,
+``aggressive_iowait`` and ``rt_max_boost``.
+
+Hot path safety
+---------------
+
+The scheduler update callback can run while rq locks are held.  Therefore v11
+changes the boost controller state reader to be lockless.
+``hydrogenx_boost_get_state()`` uses ``READ_ONCE()`` and jiffies comparisons; it
+does not take mutexes.  Sysfs writes and input events update state and schedule a
+worker for heavier SchedTune/UCLAMP/vendor bridge calls.
+
+Compression and filesystem config
+---------------------------------
+
+The patch keeps the useful config changes from the audited v10 patch:
+F2FS compression, EROFS ZIP/LZ4, zram writeback, zram LZ4 default, LZ4/LZ4HC,
+ZSTD, FQ and BBR.  LZ4K/LZ4KD/OPLUS entries remain compatibility aliases only;
+this patch does not pretend to import a real vendor codec implementation.
+
+Validation checklist
+--------------------
+
+After building, check the config::
+
+    grep -E "CPU_FREQ_GOV_HYDROGENX|CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_HYDROGENX|HYDROGENX_BOOST|F2FS_FS_COMPRESSION|EROFS_FS_ZIP|ZRAM_WRITEBACK" out/.config
+
+After booting, check runtime nodes::
+
+    cat /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_available_governors
+    cat /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/version
+    cat /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/status
+
+Expected version::
+
+    v11-hydrogen-schedutil
+
+Safe fallback
+-------------
+
+If HydrogenX behaves badly, switch policies back to schedutil::
+
+    for p in /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy*; do
+        echo schedutil > "$p/scaling_governor" 2>/dev/null
+    done
diff --git a/scripts/hydrogenx/verify-hydrogenx.sh b/scripts/hydrogenx/verify-hydrogenx.sh
new file mode 100755
index 000000000000..000000000000
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/hydrogenx/verify-hydrogenx.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+#!/system/bin/sh
+# HydrogenX v11 runtime verifier for Android shells.
+# This script is optional. The kernel patch does not require it to boot.
+
+HX=/sys/kernel/hydrogenx
+CPUFREQ=/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq
+fail=0
+
+say() { echo "[hydrogenx-verify] $*"; }
+err() { echo "[hydrogenx-verify][FAIL] $*"; fail=1; }
+warn() { echo "[hydrogenx-verify][WARN] $*"; }
+
+say "checking global controller"
+if [ ! -d "$HX" ]; then
+    err "$HX is missing; CONFIG_HYDROGENX_BOOST did not initialize"
+else
+    [ -f "$HX/version" ] && say "version=$(cat $HX/version)" || err "version node missing"
+    [ -f "$HX/builtins" ] && say "builtins=$(cat $HX/builtins)" || warn "builtins node missing"
+    [ -f "$HX/status" ] && cat "$HX/status" || warn "status node missing"
+fi
+
+say "checking cpufreq policies"
+for p in "$CPUFREQ"/policy*; do
+    [ -d "$p" ] || continue
+    govs="$p/scaling_available_governors"
+    cur="$p/scaling_governor"
+    if [ ! -f "$govs" ]; then
+        err "$p has no scaling_available_governors"
+        continue
+    fi
+    list=$(cat "$govs")
+    say "$p governors=$list"
+    echo "$list" | grep -qw hydrogenx || err "$p missing hydrogenx governor"
+    if echo "$list" | grep -qw hydrogenx; then
+        old=$(cat "$cur" 2>/dev/null)
+        echo hydrogenx > "$cur" 2>/dev/null || err "$p cannot switch to hydrogenx"
+        new=$(cat "$cur" 2>/dev/null)
+        say "$p active=$new old=$old"
+        [ -d "$p/hydrogenx" ] || warn "$p/hydrogenx tunable dir missing; global governor mode may be used"
+    fi
+ done
+
+say "checking scene pulses"
+if [ -d "$HX" ]; then
+    for n in boostpulse input_boostpulse frame_boost gpu_boost ddr_boost io_boost; do
+        if [ -f "$HX/$n" ]; then
+            echo 1 > "$HX/$n" 2>/dev/null || warn "cannot write $n"
+            say "wrote $n"
+        else
+            warn "$n node missing"
+        fi
+    done
+    [ -f "$HX/status" ] && cat "$HX/status"
+fi
+
+say "checking f2fs/erofs/zram configs from /proc/config.gz if present"
+if [ -f /proc/config.gz ]; then
+    zcat /proc/config.gz | grep -E "CONFIG_(CPU_FREQ_GOV_HYDROGENX|HYDROGENX_BOOST|F2FS_FS_COMPRESSION|EROFS_FS_ZIP|ZRAM_WRITEBACK|LZ4|ZSTD|TCP_CONG_BBR)" || warn "no matching config lines found"
+else
+    warn "/proc/config.gz unavailable"
+fi
+
+if [ "$fail" -eq 0 ]; then
+    say "PASS"
+else
+    say "FAIL"
+fi
+exit "$fail"
diff --git a/scripts/hydrogenx/apply-gaming-profile.sh b/scripts/hydrogenx/apply-gaming-profile.sh
